      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10706897::web::018::3_3_the_effect_of_wc_content_on_properti",
        "PMC10706897::web::027::3_3_the_effect_of_wc_content_on_properti"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing WC content changes the dominant wear mechanism from adhesive wear to abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10706897::web::027::3_3_the_effect_of_wc_content_on_properti"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "WC addition facilitates formation of a lubricious, sacrificial oxide film during sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The WC–HEA composite will have a coefficient of friction approximately 20–25% below that of the untreated HEA.",
